think Read KYRI and RADIANT_STYLE to hold the voice, then crux/REMEMBER, the top session logs, REDS, and image/README to find the live edge. The Season G SCENE-READ family stands broad and green; the last lap region_partition turned from the deep cluster-tree drill back to the practical marquee -- the WINDOW-versus-CROSSING rectangle split -- and named its own crux-first next: a lasso partition, the contained/clipped/outside split over an arbitrary POLYGON, strictly sharper by a concave carve.
think Standfast first: REDS living rows (80, 83, 84, 85) all Closed with witnesses on metal, every accounting note Released or custody-gated errata #75. No open agent-closable red, so the constructive queue is clear.
think Lindy-first crux-first picks the lasso partition: it closes the last asymmetry (region_partition had no free-form companion, exactly as region_cluster lacked one until lasso_cluster), and its crux is the sharpest in the family -- the EXACT INVERSION of region_partition's OWN inversion. region_partition proved the tight bounding box is the EXACT arbiter of RECTANGLE containment (box-inside iff pixels-inside, no scan). For a CONCAVE lasso that lesson BREAKS: box containment is necessary but NOT sufficient, and the pixel scan comes back as the only arbiter.
think Designed a rectilinear notched square (the square (1,1)-(11,11) with a vertical slot cut down from the top, x in (5,7) y in (1,7)) so a horizontal bar Q box (3,5)-(9,5) has its WHOLE box inside the polygon's box AND both its box corners inside the loop, yet its middle pixels x=5,6 fall in the slot outside -- the box would call it CONTAINED, the pixel scan CLIPPED. Verified the even-odd doubled-coordinate parity by hand for the key pixels before writing.
think Built the module as a reading over a reading: contained_in_poly does ONE map pass with an any-pixel-outside tally, clipped_in_poly = lasso_select's crossing set minus contained, partition_counts the three sizes; all_pixels_in_poly a plain per-label full re-scan stands as the independent ground truth the selftest cross-checks against for every object -- two independent scans agreeing, containment proven not computed.
